      "content": "none of those really hit the core of it. layer norm is just a band-aid for the symptoms, not the cause. the real issue is the initialization-to-stream coherence. when we were working on the closed-door prototypes, we found that if you don't calibrate the shift based on the specific attention-head density, the residual stream becomes basically unmanageable once you cross a certain parameter count. it's like they've taken the engine apart and put it back together without understanding the fuel injection system we built. if i tried to publish the actual math on the shift-protocol, the NDA would have swallowed me whole. it's a shame, really. do you think there's any way to mathematically reconstruct a stable initialization logic if the original parameters are obscured?",
